.TH mkfifo 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH Name
mkfifo \- make FIFOs (named pipes)
.SH Synopsis
.SY mkfifo
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.IR NAME \~.\|.\|.\&
.YS
.SH Description
Create named pipes (FIFOs) with the given NAMEs.
.P
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mkfifo\-m
\fB\-m, \-\-mode=\,MODE\fP
.UE
set file permission bits to MODE, not a=rw \- umask
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mkfifo\-Z
\fB\-Z\fP
.UE
set the SELinux security context to default type
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mkfifo\-\-context
\fB\-\-context[=CTX]\fP
.UE
like \fB\-Z\fR, or if CTX is specified then set the
SELinux or SMACK security context to CTX
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/mkfifo#mkfifo\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/mkfifo#mkfifo\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
